-- Billing set, 0000_init: the final squash (SH-12, program spec §2 "Final squash") of the stacked
-- history 0000_init .. 0008_ledger_trusted_state_read_at into one baseline. billing.squash.int-spec.ts
-- proves it builds the same catalog on Citus as the stacked files (kept in test/stacked-history).
-- Generated by drizzle-kit, then hand-edited into the sharding design's order (§4 items 2 and 6):
-- per table CREATE -> distribution -> indexes, then RLS -> grants -> policies. One statement each:
-- with local execution off, Citus builds the shards over new connections.
-- Distribution (SH-6, L-10): payments, stripe_events, outbox and the three ledger tenant tables are
-- distributed by tenant_id, colocated with app.tenant_colocation (and so with identity's tenant
-- tables); ledger_reconciliation_runs and ledger_trusted_state stay coordinator-local (no call). The
-- platform helpers are no-ops without Citus and on a re-run. No FK: a distributed table cannot
-- reference a coordinator-local one, and billing has none into identity.
-- Hand-edited to IF NOT EXISTS: the drizzle migrator creates this schema first, for billing.__drizzle_migrations.
CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS "billing";
